# v7.3 context rebase of Glymur CAMSS DTS v2 patches 1-3.
# Sources, added lines copied from these diffs and not rewritten:
#   https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261015-glymur_camss_dts-v2-1-e7b1f403146f@oss.qualcomm.com/
#   https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261015-glymur_camss_dts-v2-2-e7b1f403146f@oss.qualcomm.com/
#   https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261015-glymur_camss_dts-v2-3-e7b1f403146f@oss.qualcomm.com/
# Author of those patches: Nihal Kumar Gupta <nihal.gupta@oss.qualcomm.com>, 15 Oct 2026.
# Review: Konrad Acked-by on patch 1. Christian Cortner Tested-by for patches 1-3 on UX3607OA, with an ov02c10 node he described as CRD wiring and did not post. Konrad asked not to widen this series with A16 nodes. Jesse Casco measured cam_mclk4 at 2 mA banding on this A16 when the DMIC clock runs, and 6 mA fixing it. That override is optional and off by default. It is not in this file.
# Placement, which is the only local change: opp tables go immediately before soc@0, where patch 1's context already pointed. The CAMSS and CSIPHY block is between evacc (clock-controller@abf0000) and dispcc (clock-controller@af00000), in address order. git apply of the posted patch 1 put that block after usb_mp because the hunk context was only two lines. CCI controllers sit immediately before camss. CCI and MCLK pinctrl states sit inside &tlmm after qup_uart22_default, because v7.3 has no sdc2_default_state. Pin names, functions, registers, IRQs, clocks and drive-strength 2 are the posted values.

